\newlabel{fig:exp1}{{2}{13}{Interruption Prompt Rate (IPR) across both 50 controlled trajectories (1,500 calls, Experiment 1) and 52 real coding-agent session logs (28,087 calls, Experiment 1B). Aegis OS reduces confirmation prompts by 94.2\%--99.9\% on controlled trajectories and by 90.7\%--97.9\% on real session traces.\relax }{figure.caption.15}{}}
\@writefile{lot}{\contentsline {table}{\numberline {4}{\ignorespaces \textbf  {Experiment 1B (RQ1): Real-World Coding-Agent Session Trace Evaluation} across \textbf  {Corpus A} (52 real production coding-agent session transcripts totaling 57,923 conversation steps and 28,087 tool calls: 13,098 read/coord, 11,070 shell commands of which 4,318 [39.0\%] are compound pipelines \texttt  {\&\&}/\texttt  {|} or inline scripts \texttt  {python3 -c}, and 3,836 file edits/writes) and \textbf  {Corpus B} (5 live Aegis OS dogfooding sessions totaling 3,962 steps and 2,040 tool calls, including 68 \texttt  {workspace\_commit} and 15 ground-truth \texttt  {policy\_approve\_escalation} events), evaluated via \texttt  {scripts/e6\_real\_traces.py}.\relax }}{13}{table.caption.16}\protected@file@percent }
