\@writefile{lot}{\contentsline {table}{\numberline {9}{\ignorespaces \textbf  {Experiment 3C (RQ3): Provisioning a 1,000-file, 78 MB Tree with Real Tools} (mean time in ms; 7 trials after a warm-up, methods interleaved; physical disk consumed in parentheses when above 1 MB). Plain copy tools receive the tree without \texttt  {.git}, which Aegis OS also skips; the git-based methods inherently need the repository. External commands include 0.3--2.6 ms of process start-up; the Aegis figure is an in-process call (macOS: Table\nonbreakingspace \ref  {tab:exp3a}; Linux: range over three runs of \texttt  {aegis-os bench}). $^\dagger $XFS is a loop-backed image on btrfs and its Aegis timings are very noisy. ext4 has no reflink.\relax }}{18}{table.caption.24}\protected@file@percent }
